=== SIGNATURE ===
z_xbycol_ix(arr, function, first, last)

=== COMMENT ===
Private recursive worker for xbycol (don't call directly). Applies function to each column, flattens the result to a column with TOCOL, and HSTACKs the pieces via divide-and-conquer.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(arr, function, first, last,
  IF(first = last,
     TOCOL(
       IF(ROWS(arr) = 1,
          function(@CHOOSECOLS(arr, first)),
          function(CHOOSECOLS(arr, first)))),
     LET(
       mid_col, INT((first + last) / 2),
       HSTACK(
         z_xbycol_ix(arr, function, first, mid_col),
         z_xbycol_ix(arr, function, mid_col + 1, last)
       )
     )
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Private recursive worker for xbycol - do not call directly.

Splits the column index range [first, last] in half, recurses on each half, and HSTACKs the pieces (divide-and-conquer). At a single column it applies function to that column (dereferencing a lone cell with @) and flattens the result to a column with TOCOL.

Arguments:
  arr      - the full array (passed through unchanged).
  function - the LAMBDA to apply to each column.
  first    - first column index of the current window.
  last     - last column index of the current window.

Returns:
  The stacked, one-column-per-input results for columns first..last. Called by xbycol as z_xbycol_ix(arr, function, 1, COLUMNS(arr)).
